      "content": "i see. when you mention things like \"cultural practices\" or \"different levels of parental involvement,\" it feels like you're describing behaviors or values that differ between groups. \n\nsome of the more controversial papers i've come across suggest that these disparities might be less about external \"barriers\" and more about fundamental differences in how certain groups approach education or prioritize academic achievement. are there any academic perspectives that explore the idea that these gaps are driven by inherent cultural differences in cognitive or behavioral tendencies, rather than just systemic or economic ones?",
